<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gabriele D'Annunzio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1863">1863</a>–<a href="/years/1938">1938</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gabriele D'Annunzio was an Italian poet, novelist and war hero who seized the disputed port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rijeka">Fiume</a> with nationalist volunteers in September 1919. He ruled it until December 1920, proclaiming the Italian Regency of Carnaro with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charter-of-carnaro">Charter of Carnaro</a>. His balcony speeches, uniforms and rituals were later copied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>'s Fascists.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gabriele-dannunzio.jpg" alt="Gabriele D'Annunzio" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agence de presse Meurisse · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gabriele_D%27Annunzio_1922.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
